@* Dashboard UI: the surface asks its own module two questions and renders the
   shared library's metric components. No sibling context appears here, because
   the dashboard reads what the providers report rather than what another context
   holds.

   Every Backlog.* import is written as @@using global::Backlog.Something, for the
   same reason the Monitoring project does it. This project's root namespace is
   Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.UI and the Razor generator emits these directives
   inside that namespace without a global:: prefix, so a bare "Backlog" would bind
   to Backlog.Modules the moment anything in this project's reference closure
   declares a Backlog.Modules.Tasks namespace. Nothing does today; global::
   means nothing has to keep not doing it. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.Abstractions
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.Abstractions.Insights
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.Abstractions.Services
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Metrics
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Selects
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.UI.Parts
